naged Flink, KinesisAnalytics(V2), KPU, ParallelismPerKPU, savepoint, checkpoint, operator UID, FlinkKinesisConsumer, KinesisStreamsSource, KafkaSource, EFO, CreateApplication, UpdateApplication, CreateApplicationSnapshot, Kryo, RocksDB, EXACTLY_ONCE, watermark, CDC binlog/WAL, Glue/S3 Tables, AWS/KinesisAnalytics CloudWatch. For Iceberg, start with MSK or KDS skill and use this skill for Flink IcebergSink.\n\n\nServices: managed-flink, kinesis, kafka, msk, cloudwatch, s3, dynamodb, iam\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, migrate, design\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: streaming, real-time, data-analytics\n*","skill_name":"developing-applications-on-managed-service-for-apache-flink"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"managing-amazon-msk","skill_description":"Operates Amazon MSK Provisioned clusters (Standard and Express brokers). Required for ANY MSK Provisioned task — training data conflates Standard and Express. Covers performance, consumer lag, storage, traffic shaping; sizing Standard vs Express; Kafka client tuning; CloudWatch alarms; cluster configs; maintenance, patching, rolling restarts; topic management; MSK Replicator setup for DR and active-active/active-passive replication (same-/cross-account), including throughput and partition sizing; Streaming Tables for S3 Tables and Data Delivery for General Purpose S3 — setup, IAM, monitoring. Prefer Flink for Kafka Iceberg sink questions. Migrations: use migrate-to-msk. Triggers: MSK Provisioned, Kafka, `kafka.*`/`express.*` types, AWS/Kafka namespace, cross-cluster replication, Kafka to Iceberg on S3 Tables, Kafka to S3, lakehouse, data lake from Kafka, Kafka Connect S3 Sink or Firehose alternative. DO NOT USE for MSK Connect — search docs instead. Serverless: only S3 Tables/data delivery eligibility.\n\n\nServices: msk, kafka, cloudwatch\nTasks: troubleshoot, debug, optimize, deploy, monitor, replicate, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: streaming, data-analytics\n*","skill_name":"managing-amazon-msk"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search AWS docs for FillMsec metric definition", "parent_id": "15df998d-47bc-4168-a564-56405f9b32cf"}
